\section{Overview}

Key Punchlines:

-   A one percent increase in inter vivos transfers corresponds to a 1 (.01) percentage point increase in the probability of receiving a bequest. In other words, a 10% increase in inter vivos transfers corresponds to a 10 percentage point increase in the probability of receiving a bequest.

-   A one percent increase in inter vivos transfers corresponds to a .03% increase in the value of a bequest. In other words a 10% increase in inter vivos transfers corresponds to a .3% increase in bequest values.
-   Average value of bequests conditional on positive (excluding 0s): $85,138$
-   Average value of inter-vivos transfers conditional on positive: $30,348$

