Table 7 and Figure 3-4 describe the results from an interaction between log(inter vivos transfers) and child's education level on the value of the bequest. Only this interaction is significant, but on visual and statistical examination of the second differences of the interaction, they are not significant and confidence intervals overlap. An interaction between education and log(inter vivos transfers) on receipt of a bequest was also not significant. These results together suggest that a child's education level does not have a statistically meaningful affect on the focal relationship between inter vivos transfers and bequests. Figure 1 does suggest that the association between inter vivos transfers and bequests is stronger for the less than HS group, however these differences are not meaningfully different than the other education categories.

