Table 8 and Figure 5-6 present coefficients and graphical presentations of an interaction between log(Inter-Vivos Transfers) and whether the child is a homeowner. The interaction, when modeling the association with receiving a bequest is statistically significant based on an F-test between models $(p < 0.01)$ and the first and second differences of the interaction are also significant (diff $\ = 0.006$). In other words, being a homeowner matters for the relationship between inter vivos transfers and the probability a child receives a bequest, but does not affect the value of that bequest in a meaningful way.

